{
  "_comment": [
    "Captured FLEET SAMPLES (Milestone 5E) — one measurement per vehicle, in the",
    "shape aggregate.ts consumes. This is what makes fleet aggregation and the",
    "coverage disclosure exercisable with no database, the same way",
    "telemetry-series.json exercises series.ts.",
    "",
    "PROVENANCE. Every entry is REAL. Each is the latest reading of one vehicle,",
    "read through the same projection the engine runs — so the placeholder floors",
    "and the CAN signal timestamps are already applied. No value was altered and",
    "none was invented. Captured 2026-08-03 from the loaded database, whose",
    "population is 70 vehicles.",
    "",
    "WHY THESE THREE QUANTITIES. They span the whole coverage range this design",
    "has to report honestly:",
    "",
    "- state_of_charge   70 of 70 vehicles contribute. Full coverage, and the",
    "                    contributing measurements span 0.3 days.",
    "- pack_temperature  69 of 70. One vehicle's latest CAN row carries no usable",
    "                    battery_temp, so the coverage gap is REAL rather than",
    "                    constructed — and the span is 59.4 DAYS, because the CAN",
    "                    payload is a last-known-value snapshot and one vehicle's",
    "                    latest temperature was measured in April while another's",
    "                    was measured in June. This is the fixture that proves the",
    "                    span is load-bearing.",
    "- battery_health    1 of 70. The battery dataset covers a single vehicle, so",
    "                    a fleet aggregate over it is honest about resting on one",
    "                    measurement rather than confident about the fleet.",
    "",
    "`nonContributors` carries the REASON each excluded vehicle was excluded, so a",
    "test can assert that a missing member is reported rather than counted as zero."
  ],
